{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538488-what-is-the-origins-of-the-giovanni-family-before-they-become-vampires","id":1538488,"title":"what is the origins of the giovanni family, before they become vampires","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-07-12T13:50:39-07:00","id":1538488,"title":"what is the origins of the giovanni family, before they become vampires","content":"i don't actually know","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-12T13:58:20-07:00","id":1538489,"title":"","content":"I forget all the details because it\u2019s been a while since I\u2019ve read the clan books or the Giovanni Chronicle but iirc:<br /> <br /> \u2022They may have existed since Roman times as keepers of an ancient Roman (probably actually Etruscan, if true) necromancy rites but imo that\u2019s probably a Concession of Constantine style medieval forgery to artificially add prestige to their lineage <br /> \u2022Regardless circa Venice in the late Middle Ages (I agree with others that Genoa or Milan might have been better candidates, but whatever) they were a prominent family of ambitious merchant-princes who secretly practiced necromancy and black-magic which they used to facilitate their commercial endeavors<br /> \u2022It was the combination of their business skills and necromancy that ostensibly drew the notice of the Cappadocian\u2019s and which led to the story of the Giovanni coup that we know today <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-12T14:34:45-07:00","id":1538491,"title":"","content":"Cliff notes version is that the Giovanni were a merchantile family from Rome with necromancy interests and were called Jovian at the time and it wouldn't be to shocking if members of the family were embraced by Ventrue and Lasombra clans. If I recall some powerful spectre had an interest in the family and kept an eye on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-12T15:05:06-07:00","id":1538496,"title":"","content":"thank you lots","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-13T09:52:25-07:00","id":1538524,"title":"","content":"I should also add that the Giovanni necromancy interests garnered the attention of Cappadocius in the early 11th century and he embraced Augustus in 1005 over the objection of Japeth and Lady Constancia who saw him for what he was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-13T10:25:57-07:00","id":1538526,"title":"","content":"Don't forget that they are also involved heavily with an ancient wraith or spirit named Dis Pater before they became vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5617-vendrin","name":"Vendrin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-13T10:53:35-07:00","id":1538528,"title":"","content":"So I did recall correctly that ancient spirit was involved in the doings of the Giovanni family.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-13T18:36:30-07:00","id":1538546,"title":"","content":"What's more relevant in their history, as far as lore goes, is that modern Necromancy comes from their practices, not from Cappadocian Mortis.<br /> <br /> So for millennia the Cappadocian did research only on the effects of death on this side of the Shroud, while this family from the Italian Latio was possibly the most advanced (non-awakened) researchers of ghosts, how to contact and how to bind them.<br /> <br /> Bringing the Giovanni into the clan was an extremely important move in the development of the clan's Discipline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}